The '''''Alianza Anónima Anticomunista''''' ({{Literal translation|Anonymous Anti-Communist Alliance}}; '''AAA''') was a Baliscan [[W:Far-right politics|far-right]] [[W:Paramilitary|paramilitary organisation]] active from 1919 to 1930, primarily in rural [[Bayara]] but also across [[Cerdanya]] and [[Hesperia]]. The AAA, largely made up of dispossessed landowners, capitalists and other wealthy elites, engaged in [[W:Right-wing terrorism|terrorism]] and violent struggle against the [[Baliscan Revolution|revolutionary regime]] taking shape. 

Throughout it's two decades of activity, it targeted migrants, artists, priests, intellectuals, leftist politicians, students, historians and union members, as well as issuing threats and carrying out [[W:Extrajudicial killing|extrajudicial killings]] and [[W:Forced disappearances|forced disappearances]]. 

